# Milestone git workflow

Use one branch per milestone. Merge into `main` only when that milestone is finished.

## Branch naming

- `milestone-2`, `milestone-3`, `milestone-4`, … (hyphen, no spaces, no `cursor/` prefix)

## Start a milestone

1. Update and check out `main`
2. Create the milestone branch from `main`
3. Do all work and commits on that branch only

```bash
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git checkout -b milestone-N
```

## Finish a milestone

1. Confirm the milestone work is complete and committed
2. Merge into `main`
3. Push `main` (and optionally push the milestone branch)

```bash
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git merge milestone-N
git push origin main
git push origin milestone-N
```

## Rules

- Do not commit directly to `main` during a milestone
- Do not push incomplete milestone work to `main`
- Keep commit messages professional and plain: what changed, in simple words
- Never commit `.env` or secrets
- Author identity stays the user's git name/email (not Cursor)
